  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 937 PM CST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nA powerful trough will be digging into the eastern CONUS Wednesday\ninto Thursday. This will bring a sharp cold front through Wednesday\nnight or Thursday. Only a low chance of a shower or thunderstorm\nexist with the front before blustery north-northwest winds occur \nbehind the front. After highs in the 60s Thursday, overnight lows \nwill dip into the lower to middle 30s Thursday Night. Highs on Friday\nwill only reach the lower 50s in valleys and upper 40s atop the \nCumberland Plateau. This will be about ~15 degrees below normal. The \nfirst widespread freeze of the season will take place Friday night \ninto Saturday morning with lows in the upper 20s to around 30. High \npressure will shift southeast into the Gulf States late Saturday, \nwith overnight lows in the upper 20s to lower 30s.",
